# TeleMed Project Structure

## Monorepo Layout

TeleMed uses a **Turborepo monorepo** with pnpm workspaces:

```
apps/       - Application code (mobile, api)
packages/   - Shared libraries (shared, ts-config, eslint-config)
tooling/    - Build and dev tooling
supabase/   - Database migrations
.cursor/    - AI rules and subagents
```

## Package Naming

- All packages use the `@telemed/` scope
- App packages: `@telemed/mobile`, `@telemed/api`
- Shared packages: `@telemed/shared`, `@telemed/ts-config`, `@telemed/eslint-config`

## Import Conventions

- Use path aliases configured in tsconfig: `@/` maps to `src/`
- Cross-package imports use `@telemed/shared` (workspace dependency)
- Never use relative imports across package boundaries beyond one level
- Prefer barrel exports (index.ts) in shared packages

## File Naming

- Components: PascalCase (`SignInScreen.tsx`, `ProfessionalCard.tsx`)
- Utilities: kebab-case or camelCase (`api-utils.ts`, `tokenCache.ts`)
- Types: camelCase matching domain (`database.ts`, `api.ts`)
- Route files: Expo Router conventions (`[id].tsx`, `_layout.tsx`, `index.tsx`)

## Adding New Packages

Run from the monorepo root:
```bash
pnpm turbo gen workspace
```
Or manually create the package and add to `pnpm-workspace.yaml`.
